Here is the complete suite for your presentation. I've engineered the HTML, CSS, and JS to reflect the rigorous, high-stakes nature of the CLAVIS protocol, using a high-tech "secure enclave" aesthetic (deep slates, cryptographic greens, and biometric blues).

I have integrated your specific academic credentials, the Australian socio-economic context (Optus/Medibank, CDR), and the deep technical architecture (Merkle Trees, Encrypted Document Store, ISO 18013-5) straight into the slides.

1. index.html

Save this as index.html. It contains the semantic structure of the slides and incorporates the image tags to trigger visual aids for your audience.

HTML
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>CLAVIS Protocol Presentation</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>

    <div class="slide-container title-slide" id="slide1" data-short-title="CLAVIS Protocol">
        <div class="title-layout">
            <div class="hardware-badge"><i class="fa-solid fa-microchip"></i> Hardware-Bound SSI</div>
            <h1 class="hero-title">
                <span class="hero-primary">CLAVIS</span>
                <span class="hero-secondary">Cryptographic Linked Attestation & Verifiable Identity System</span>
            </h1>
            <p class="subtitle">A framework for decentralized identity, semantic interoperability, and zero-trust verification.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="slide-container about-slide" id="slide2" data-short-title="Presenter">
        <h2 class="slide-title">Principal Architect</h2>
        <div class="content-area">
            <div class="about-grid">
                <section class="about-profile presenter">
                    <div class="profile-details">
                        <span class="profile-tag">Author & Lead</span>
                        <h3 class="profile-name">Dr. Oleksii Konashevych</h3>
                        <div class="profile-fields">
                            <div class="profile-field">
                                <span class="profile-label">Academic Credentials</span>
                                <p class="profile-value">Doctor of Philosophy in Law, Science and Technology</p>
                                <p class="profile-description">University of Bologna. Specialization in public blockchain applications and digital government architectures.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="profile-field">
                                <span class="profile-label">Focus</span>
                                <p class="profile-description">Bridging the gap between cryptographic protocols, Australian regulatory frameworks (CDR, Privacy Act), and high-efficiency technical implementations.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="slide-container" id="slide3" data-short-title="The Crisis">
        <h2 class="slide-title">The Digital Identity Paradox</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">Australia's current verification architecture is broken, leading to compounding systemic failures.</p>
        <div class="content-area">
                        <div class="tiled-content">
                <div class="tile alert-tile">
                    <div class="icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-database"></i></div>
                    <h3>The "Honey Pot" Crisis</h3>
                    <p>Centralized storage of PII (Optus, Medibank) creates high-value targets. We are currently storing "the proof" (scans) rather than verifying the cryptographic claim.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tile">
                    <div class="icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-hourglass-half"></i></div>
                    <h3>Administrative Friction</h3>
                    <p>The "productivity tax" of manual data entry in healthcare and government costs billions annually, introducing severe human-error risks.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tile alert-tile">
                    <div class="icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-eye"></i></div>
                    <h3>Privacy Over-sharing</h3>
                    <p>Verification is currently all-or-nothing. Users surrender massive amounts of irrelevant PII simply to prove a single attribute (e.g., age or license validity).</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="slide-container" id="slide4" data-short-title="No-DB Architecture">
        <h2 class="slide-title">Encrypted Document Store</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">Abandoning the monolithic database. Moving identity storage strictly to the Edge.</p>
        <div class="content-area">
            <div class="two-column">
                <div>
                    <h3>Zero-Centralization (No-DB)</h3>
                    <p>CLAVIS rejects traditional SQL/relational mappings for identity. We utilize a hybrid <strong>Index + Container</strong> architecture.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Meta-Index:</strong> Handled by Android <code>EncryptedSharedPreferences</code>. Stores only non-PII headers to build the UI.</li>
                        <li><strong>Encrypted Blobs:</strong> Every document (passport, diploma) is an isolated, hardware-encrypted JSON-LD file.</li>
                        <li><strong>Right to be Forgotten:</strong> Achieved through physical file deletion, leaving no residual logs in a central database.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="architecture-diagram">
                        <div class="arch-box tee">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-microchip"></i>
                            <span>Hardware TEE / StrongBox</span>
                            <div class="arch-key"><i class="fa-solid fa-key"></i> Non-exportable Key</div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="arch-arrow"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-down"></i> Gated by Biometrics</div>
                        <div class="arch-box native-api">
                            <span>Jetpack Security Crypto API</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="arch-blobs">
                            <div class="blob"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-prescription"></i> Medical.json</div>
                            <div class="blob"><i class="fa-solid fa-passport"></i> Identity.json</div>
                            <div class="blob"><i class="fa-solid fa-building-columns"></i> Fin.json</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="slide-container" id="slide5" data-short-title="Zero-Mapping">
        <h2 class="slide-title">Semantic Interoperability</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">"We speak the language of your systems. Zero mapping required."</p>
        <div class="content-area">
                        <div class="two-column tiled">
                <div>
                    <h3>Industry Vocabularies</h3>
                    <p>CLAVIS documents are native <strong>JSON-LD Verifiable Credentials (W3C)</strong>. We do not enforce proprietary field names.</p>
                    <p><strong>Health:</strong> Native <em>HL7 FHIR</em> Resources.<br>
                    <strong>Finance:</strong> <em>ISO 20022</em> and Australian CDR schemas.<br>
                    <strong>General:</strong> <em>Schema.org</em>.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>The Integration Pitch</h3>
                    <p>For Verifiers (Hospitals, Banks), integration cost drops by 90%. When CLAVIS delivers a payload, developers don't parse a custom API—they feed the payload directly into their existing FHIR or CDR compliant engines.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="slide-container" id="slide6" data-short-title="Selective Disclosure">
        <h2 class="slide-title">Surgical Privacy: Merkle Trees</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">Fulfilling the principle of Data Minimization without losing cryptographic trust.</p>
        <div class="content-area">
            <div class="two-column">
                <div class="merkle-visual">
                                        <div class="tree-root">Signed Root (Issuer)</div>
                    <div class="tree-branches">
                        <div class="branch exposed">Name <span>(Shared)</span></div>
                        <div class="branch exposed">Photo <span>(Shared)</span></div>
                        <div class="branch hidden">Address <span>(Hidden)</span></div>
                        <div class="branch hidden">DOB <span>(Hidden)</span></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Selective Disclosure</h3>
                    <p>Instead of sharing an entire document, CLAVIS generates a <strong>Merkle Proof</strong> for only the required fields.</p>
                    <h3>The Visual Anchor</h3>
                    <p>Digital proofs require physical binding. The user's photo is a cryptographically signed leaf in the Merkle Tree. The Verifier's terminal confirms the root signature, then displays the photo for human-in-the-loop verification.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="slide-container" id="slide7" data-short-title="Proximity Sync">
        <h2 class="slide-title">The Physical Gateway (ISO 18013-5)</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">Replacing plastic cards in offline environments.</p>
        <div class="content-area">
                        <div class="tiled-content">
                <div class="tile">
                    <div class="icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-wifi"></i><i class="fa-solid fa-slash" style="position:absolute; margin-left:-35px; color:#ef4444;"></i></div>
                    <h3>Offline by Design</h3>
                    <p>Works in hospital basements or remote checkpoints. No internet required for the Holder to prove identity.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tile">
                    <div class="icon"><i class="fa-brands fa-nfc-symbol"></i></div>
                    <h3>NFC "Tap & Go"</h3>
                    <p>Device Engagement happens instantly. Tap the terminal, authorize with biometrics, and the presentation is securely transmitted.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tile">
                    <div class="icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-qrcode"></i></div>
                    <h3>QR + BLE</h3>
                    <p>For systems lacking NFC, a dynamic QR code establishes a secure Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) tunnel for heavy data transfer.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="slide-container" id="slide8" data-short-title="Non-Repudiation">
        <h2 class="slide-title">The Trust Protocol & Non-Repudiation</h2>
        <div class="content-area">
            <div class="two-column">
                <div>
                    <p>Verification is a two-way street. In CLAVIS, the Verifier must digitally sign their request for data.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Dynamic Requests:</strong> For High-Trust entities (Banks, Hospitals). Every request is signed in real-time with a nonce and strict expiration (preventing replay attacks).</li>
                        <li><strong>Static Manifests:</strong> For Standard-Trust entities (E-commerce). A one-time signed schema lowering the barrier to entry.</li>
                        <li><strong>Immutable Audit:</strong> The Holder's device saves the signed request as a "Receipt of Demand," establishing legal non-repudiation if the Verifier misuses the data.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="terminal-box">
                    <div class="terminal-header">Request_Payload.jwt</div>
                    <pre><code>{
  "aud": "did:clavis:user:123",
  "iss": "did:clavis:org:st-vincents",
  "nonce": "8f7e6d5c",
  "exp": 1711681200,
  "claims": {
    "fhir_patient": ["criticalAllergies", "bloodType"]
  },
  "retention_policy": "ephemeral"
}</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="slide-container" id="slide9" data-short-title="Discourse">
        <h2 class="slide-title">Academic & Technological Positioning</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">How CLAVIS maps to the global Self-Sovereign Identity (SSI) landscape.</p>
        <div class="content-area">
            <div class="table-layout">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Layer / Concept</th>
                            <th>Global Standard</th>
                            <th>CLAVIS Implementation</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Trust Architecture</strong></td>
                            <td>Trust over IP (ToIP)</td>
                            <td>Operates at Layer 3 (Credential Exchange) with hardware-gated Level 3 Assurance.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Data Model</strong></td>
                            <td>W3C Verifiable Credentials</td>
                            <td>JSON-LD strict compliance with embedded industry vocabularies.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Storage</strong></td>
                            <td>Encrypted Data Vaults (EDV)</td>
                            <td>Local-First Confidential Storage via Android Keystore system.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Transmission</strong></td>
                            <td>OID4VP / ISO 18013-5</td>
                            <td>Supports both remote OpenID protocols and offline Proximity exchanges.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="slide-container" id="slide10" data-short-title="Q&A">
        <div class="qa-layout">
            <h2>Questions?</h2>
            <p>Thank you for your attention.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <button id="menu-toggle" onclick="toggleSidebar()">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-bars"></i>
    </button>

    <div id="sidebar">
        <div class="sidebar-header">
            <div class="sidebar-actions">
                <button id="reorder-toggle" class="sidebar-btn icon-btn" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Reorder slides" title="Reorder slides" hidden>
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i>
                </button>
                <button id="reorder-save" class="sidebar-btn is-primary" type="button" hidden>Save</button>
                <button id="reorder-cancel" class="sidebar-btn" type="button" hidden>Cancel</button>
                <button id="reorder-reset" class="sidebar-btn" type="button" hidden>Reset</button>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div id="sidebar-reorder-hint" class="sidebar-reorder-hint" hidden></div>
        <div id="sidebar-status" class="sidebar-status" hidden></div>
        <div id="sidebar-thumbnails"></div>
    </div>

    <div id="dots-container"></div>

    <div class="nav-btn nav-up" onclick="prevSlide()"><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-up"></i></div>
    <div class="nav-btn nav-down" onclick="nextSlide()"><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></div>

    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

2. style.css

Save this as style.css. I've shifted the color palette to deep slates (#0f172a), cryptographic greens (#10b981), and secure indigos (#6366f1) to reflect the cybersecurity and SSI nature of your project.

CSS
/* 1. THE SETUP */
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
[hidden] { display: none !important; }
p { margin: 0; margin-bottom: 15px; }

body {
    background-color: #020617; /* Very dark slate */
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    height: 100vh;
    width: 100vw;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
}

/* 1.1 SLIDE CONTAINER */
.slide-container {
    align-items: flex-start;
    background-color: transparent;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    height: 720px;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    padding: 60px;
    position: relative;
    width: 1280px;
    z-index: 10;
}
.slide-container > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

/* 2. CONSISTENT TYPOGRAPHY */
.slide-container h1, .slide-container h2, .slide-container h3 {
    color: #F8FAFC;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
}
.slide-container h1 { font-size: 70px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -1px; }
.slide-container .slide-title {
    color: #10B981; /* Cryptographic Green */
    font-size: 46px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    text-align: left;
    width: 100%;
    letter-spacing: -1px;
}
.slide-container h3 {
    color: #6366F1; /* Secure Indigo */
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
}
.slide-container p, .slide-container li, .slide-container th, .slide-container td {
    color: #CBD5E1;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.6;
}
.slide-container .subtitle {
    color: #94A3B8;
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: -25px 0 30px 0;
}
.slide-container .content-area {
    align-items: center;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    flex-grow: 1;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 100%;
}

/* Title Slide */
.title-layout {
    align-items: center;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 100%;
    text-align: center;
    width: 100%;
}
.hardware-badge {
    background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.3);
    color: #34D399;
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
}
.hero-title { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 30px; }
.hero-primary {
    font-size: 140px;
    font-weight: 700;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #10B981, #3B82F6);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -3px;
}
.hero-secondary { font-size: 35px; font-weight: 500; color: #F8FAFC; opacity: 0.9; }

/* Two Column Layout */
.two-column {
    align-items: center;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    gap: 60px;
    width: 100%;
}
.two-column.tiled { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; align-items: stretch; }
.two-column.tiled > div {
    background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 1px solid #1E293B;
    padding: 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
}
.two-column ul { list-style: none; padding-left: 0; }
.two-column li { margin-bottom: 20px; position: relative; padding-left: 30px; }
.two-column li::before {
    content: '\f058'; /* Check circle */
    font-family: "Font Awesome 6 Free";
    font-weight: 900;
    color: #10B981;
    position: absolute; left: 0; font-size: 22px; top: 2px;
}

/* Tiled Content (Icons) */
.tiled-content { display: flex; gap: 30px; width: 100%; justify-content: center; align-items: stretch;}
.tile {
    background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);
    border: 1px solid #1E293B;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 40px 30px;
    flex: 1;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
}
.tile .icon { color: #6366F1; font-size: 45px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.alert-tile { border-color: rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.3); }
.alert-tile .icon { color: #F43F5E; }

/* Table Layout */
.table-layout { width: 100%; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.8); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #1E293B; overflow: hidden; }
.table-layout table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
.table-layout th, .table-layout td { border-bottom: 1px solid #1E293B; padding: 20px 30px; text-align: left; }
.table-layout th { background-color: #0F172A; color: #10B981; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; }
.table-layout td strong { color: #F8FAFC; }

/* Custom Visuals for CLAVIS */
.architecture-diagram { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 15px; }
.arch-box { background: #0F172A; border: 2px solid #3B82F6; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; width: 100%; text-align: center; font-weight: 600; color: #fff;}
.arch-box.tee { border-color: #10B981; background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.1); }
.arch-key { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #34D399; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.5); padding: 5px; border-radius: 6px;}
.arch-arrow { color: #94A3B8; font-size: 16px; }
.arch-blobs { display: flex; gap: 10px; width: 100%; }
.blob { flex: 1; background: #1E293B; padding: 15px 10px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 16px; border: 1px solid #334155;}

.merkle-visual { background: #0F172A; padding: 30px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #1E293B; text-align: center;}
.tree-root { background: #10B981; color: #000; padding: 10px; border-radius: 8px; font-weight:bold; margin-bottom: 20px;}
.tree-branches { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; }
.branch { padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 18px; border: 1px solid #334155; }
.branch.exposed { border-color: #3B82F6; background: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.1); color: #fff;}
.branch.hidden { border-color: #F43F5E; background: rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.1); opacity: 0.5; text-decoration: line-through;}

.terminal-box { background: #020617; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #1E293B; overflow: hidden; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;}
.terminal-header { background: #0F172A; padding: 10px 15px; color: #94A3B8; font-size: 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1E293B;}
.terminal-box pre { padding: 20px; margin: 0; color: #34D399; font-size: 16px; overflow-x: auto; }

/* Q&A Layout */
.qa-layout { margin: auto; text-align: center; }
.qa-layout h2 { color: #10B981; font-size: 90px; margin-bottom: 30px; }
.qa-layout p { font-size: 28px; }

/* ABOUT PROFILE */
.about-grid { display: grid; width: 100%; max-width: 800px;}
.about-profile {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.9), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6));
    border: 1px solid rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.3);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: 40px;
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
}
.profile-tag { color: #34D399; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; display: block; margin-bottom: 10px;}
.profile-name { font-size: 40px; margin-bottom: 30px; color: #fff;}
.profile-field { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding-bottom: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;}
.profile-field:last-child { border: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;}
.profile-label { color: #94A3B8; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; font-weight: 600;}
.profile-value { font-size: 24px; color: #F8FAFC; margin-top: 5px; font-weight: 500;}

/* PRESENTATION MODE STYLES */
#presentation-viewport { position: relative; width: 100vw; height: 100vh; overflow: hidden; perspective: 1000px; }
.slide-wrapper {
    position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;
    display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;
    opacity: 0; visibility: hidden; transition: opacity 0.8s ease, transform 0.8s ease;
    z-index: 1; transform: translateY(100%);
    background-color: #020617;
}
.slide-wrapper::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; top: -50%; left: -50%; width: 200%; height: 200%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 75% 25%, rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.05) 0%, transparent 40%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 25% 75%, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.05) 0%, transparent 40%);
    z-index: 0; pointer-events: none;
}
.slide-wrapper.prev { transform: translateY(-100%); opacity: 0; visibility: hidden; }
.slide-wrapper.active { opacity: 1; visibility: visible; z-index: 10; transform: translateY(0); }
.slide-wrapper.next { transform: translateY(100%); opacity: 0; visibility: hidden; }
.slide-container { transform-origin: center center; position: absolute !important; }

/* Nav Buttons & Dots */
.nav-btn {
    position: fixed; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 50;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); color: #fff; width: 50px; height: 50px;
    border-radius: 50%; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;
    cursor: pointer; transition: background 0.3s; font-size: 24px;
}
.nav-btn:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.3); }
.nav-up { top: 20px; }
.nav-down { bottom: 20px; }

#menu-toggle {
    position: fixed; top: 14px; left: 30px; z-index: 1001; background: none; border: none;
    color: #F8FAFC; font-size: 28px; cursor: pointer; transition: transform 0.3s;
}
#menu-toggle:hover { transform: scale(1.1); }
#dots-container { position: fixed; left: 40px; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); z-index: 990; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; transition: opacity 0.3s, left 0.4s; }
body.drawer-open #dots-container { opacity: 0; left: -50px; pointer-events: none; }
